cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite version 0.1.0 once released; before release, cite the exact commit used."
title: "Convergence of iterated SOCP refinement for CAZAC feasibility"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/convex-framework-cazac"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/convex-framework-cazac"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Proofs and reference code for an iterated second-order cone programming
  method for coupled CAZAC feasibility. The work proves global convergence to
  a fixed point, constructs exposed non-CAZAC fixed points, proves finite local
  arrival under a regularity condition, and computes that condition exactly at
  Zadoff--Chu tuples for every length.
keywords:
  - CAZAC sequence
  - Zadoff--Chu sequence
  - second-order cone programming
  - iterated linear optimization
  - Fourier analysis
  - semialgebraic optimization
